# Lesson 1 — say "hello"
#
# Welcome to Boxy! This is your first program.
# 'say' tells the computer to print something on the screen.
#
# The thing in quotes is called a "string" — a piece of text.

say "hello, world"

# Try changing the words inside the quotes and run the lesson again:
#     ./boxy lesson 1
#
# What happens if you forget the quotes? Try it and see what Boxy says.
